kstabs  even the player in this trailer plays  locked off a lot of the time  but for the sake of new players i think  being able to angle your role  into enemies while locked on is a huge  quality of life improvement that  they should consider if it's not already  in the game finally the presentation of  the trailer deserves a bit of criticism  it is weird that the player one hits  everything even through shields  the game will not play this way enemies  in the tutorial don't die this easily  so it was kind of weird that they chose  to present it this way  now there are more good things to say  than bad the updated music sounds great  and even the narration here is new  [Music]  so they're either bringing on a new  voice acting cast  or they're re-recording the original  voice actors i can't quite tell with the  maiden but  whoever she is she's doing a great job  with her lines and  that fills me with hope the sound design  is seeing huge changes too  i like the whisper of spirits when you  absorb souls  and your character actually makes a lot  of noise while they're running and  fighting now  this sort of character immersion is  interesting i worry that it might be a  bit distracting but i'll have to see how  it feels  but one thing i do hope that they do is  to have the character exertion  sounds in human form but to have the  character be quiet  in soul form enemies also seem more  vocal which  can be good for your sort of 3d  awareness of them but if you do see them  you'll notice that their faces are  contorting  as they attack and that their weapons  and shields now drop from their lifeless  hands once they're defeated  either that or they ricochet around the  room like crazy  it's one of the two backstabs now  feature a cruel  twist which i like and reposts pick up  your enemy and slam them down  which i like a little bit less but it's  okay overall  the trend here if you're noticing it is  that there is a lot more of our  character on display  here and i'm c